WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.902
-Hello, Congresswoman Demings.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.671
-Good evening.
It's great to be with you.

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:09.308
-Thank you so much for coming on
the show and talking to me.

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:11.511
I want to get into everything
with you

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.647
because you're such
an interesting person.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:17.082
I read somewhere that you held

00:00:17.082 --> 00:00:19.852
your first office
in sixth grade.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:21.421
Do you know what
I'm talking about?

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.056
-Oh, my God.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.691
So, look, first through
fifth grade,

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:29.361
I went to an all-black school,
first through fifth.

00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:31.997
And then in sixth grade,
our school was integrated,

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:36.035
so I was transferred to a school
that was much closer to my home.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.704
I grew up in
a rural part of Jacksonville.

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:42.041
And I was selected
to be a school patrol.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.976
And, Jimmy, I took my job

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:47.680
as a school patrol
very, very seriously.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.351
It was supposed to be limited to
helping children, you know,

00:00:52.351 --> 00:00:55.421
maybe cross the street
or cross the parking lot,

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:58.190
and just standing there
with my orange badge on,

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.325
looking official.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.928
But I really carried my job
to the bus.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.196
And if kids were misbehav--
[ Laughs ]

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:05.832
-Oh, yeah!

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.032
You put them in their place!

00:01:07.032 --> 00:01:08.801
I love it! Oh, my God!

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.803
And look at you now. See, kids?

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.505
-I'm surprised they didn't do
a stakeout and wait for me

00:01:13.505 --> 00:01:15.274
on the playground or something.

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:16.909
-Yeah. I know, yeah.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.646
-Look now.
-Look at you now.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.814
With everything that's going on,

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:24.017
I mean, there's so much
happening in this world.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:29.021
And gosh, I just want to
first off and say I think

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:32.492
you've done a great job
with everything that's going on,

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.727
with Black Lives Matter

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.996
kind of putting you
in an interesting position.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.931
-What happened to
George Floyd --

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:41.801
and let me say this as
a former law enforcement officer

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:45.204
who did the job 27 years --
I grew up

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.307
in the Orlando police
department,

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.807
worked my way up
through the ranks

00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:51.878
to become their first woman
chief of police.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:55.048
It was a job that I loved
and a job that I felt like

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:57.416
I was really
making a difference.

00:01:57.416 --> 00:01:58.885
-Sure.
-But what I do know is

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.754
what happened to George Floyd
was brutal.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.290
It was senseless. It was murder.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.192
And the persons responsible

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.862
are being and should be held
accountable.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:13.432
What happened to Breonna Taylor,
we need to look at our policies

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:16.268
at law enforcement agencies
all over this country.

00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:18.904
No-knock warrants,
I'm very familiar with them.

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:21.674
They always been high-risk.
They're dangerous.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.510
And so when we look at
the things that we're doing

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.914
or proposing in the George Floyd
Justice and Policing Act,

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:31.084
we're dealing with, you know,
who we hire.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.351
We're dealing with training.

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:34.053
We're dealing with policy

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:36.622
and trying to develop
a national standard.

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:40.593
So whether you're a 10-person
agency in a small town

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:44.564
or a 36,000-person agency
in a big city,

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:48.001
there will be some national
standards that really will help

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.669
to govern how
police departments operate.

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:52.037
And that's a good thing.

00:02:52.037 --> 00:02:54.173
-All those years
as police chief,

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:56.709
is there something
that you're most proud of?

00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:01.214
-When I was appointed chief
at the end of 2007,

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.716
crime was at an all-time high
in Orlando.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:07.120
I knew that
if I had not been successful

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.588
in reducing the crime rate,

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.089
we know what people
would have said.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:13.125
"First woman chief, oh, my God,
she can't handle that job.

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:15.128
And my God,
she's a black woman too."

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.196
Perhaps they may have said that.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:19.132
But instead of focusing on
the crisis,

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.000
I chose to focus on
the opportunity.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.869
I reorganized the department.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:26.338
I disbanded some units
that were pretty dysfunctional.

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:30.075
And we worked very closely
with our community,

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:34.881
and we were able to reduce
violent crime by over 40%.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.784
-Wow.
-I'm very proud of that.

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:41.820
-Is there something you wish
you did a better job of?

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.523
-You know, as a public servant,

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:48.494
and I won't just limit it
to police work,

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:52.198
I would hope that every public
servant would say to themselves,

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:57.269
when asked that question, "Yeah,
I wish I would have done more."

00:03:57.269 --> 00:04:00.806
I really wish I would have
focused more on training

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:02.107
within the police department.

00:04:02.107 --> 00:04:04.944
We focused a lot on training.
Don't get me wrong.

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.546
We trained in some areas

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:10.182
four times more
than the state required.

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:12.852
But in terms of
de-escalation training,

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:16.723
one of the things that I used to
say to the men and women

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:19.759
all the time when I was
the chief was that

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:23.329
number one, you have a lot of
equipment around your waist.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:27.600
The best weapon that you have is
the good brain that you have.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.835
-Yes.
-"Use it. Always use it."

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:32.605
Our ability
to communicate with people.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:37.109
When we talk about de-escalation
skills, that's all that is.

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:39.512
It might have a fancy name,
but it's the ability

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:44.683
to not be rushed,
not respond to the next call

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:47.553
before you finish this one,
but really take your time

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.789
and use the best weapon
that you have been issued,

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:54.693
your brain and the gift of gab
to de-escalate the situation.

00:04:54.693 --> 00:04:56.028
Now let me say this.

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:57.497
You can't do it on everybody.

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:59.899
There are some people who are
just looking for the fight.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:02.402
Right? And if you show up
in a police uniform,

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.770
that's the one
they've been looking for.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.906
-Yeah.
-But to have focused more

00:05:07.906 --> 00:05:10.909
on de-escalation training,
I think, is always a win-win.

00:05:10.909 --> 00:05:13.712
And that's definitely something
that we are doing

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:16.448
with the George Floyd
Justice and Policing Act.

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:18.151
And I believe
that's a good thing.

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:21.053
-Before we go, and thank you
so much again for doing this,

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:22.121
I know you're very busy.

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:25.257
Congresswoman, you are
on the short list

00:05:25.257 --> 00:05:28.528
of maybe being
the vice president.

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:33.466
As the little girl who is the,
you know, the school patrol,

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:39.404
the 11-year-old Val, would you
ever think this is possible?

00:05:39.404 --> 00:05:43.208
-What my parents helped me
to see or what they made

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:48.147
their seven children
and their baby daughter believe

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:51.951
was that only in America
it's possible.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:53.753
And if we look historically,

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:56.655
America has let us down
in some areas.

00:05:56.655 --> 00:06:01.160
But as a nation, we've always
seemed to have the ability

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.330
to stand up and get it right.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.998
Whether that's
the women's right movement,

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:09.335
the civil rights movement,
the voting rights movement,

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:12.037
marriage equality
and equal rights,

00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:15.508
we've always had the ability
to get it right.

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:19.311
And so I do believe that
only in America

00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:22.515
can that little black girl
who grew up the daughter

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:26.352
of a maid and a janitor,
served as the school patrol,

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:31.490
be on a short list for Vice
President of the United States.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.460
I'm honored and humbled by
the possibility.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:38.564
-Congresswoman, thank you
so much for coming on our show

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:39.865
and talking to me.

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:41.767
I would love to
talk to you more.

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:44.904
And I would love to see you in
person one day, hopefully soon.

